Source: duckdb
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Krysztal Huang <krysztal.huang@outlook.com>
Build-Depends:
 clang,
 cmake,
 debhelper-compat (= 13),
 git,
 libcurl4-openssl-dev,
 libmariadb-dev,
 libpq-dev,
 libssl-dev,
 ninja-build,
 python3,
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Homepage: {{SOURCE_GIT}}
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: duckdb
Architecture: any
Depends: ca-certificates, ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: fast in-process analytical database engine (CLI)
 DuckDB is a high-performance analytical database system. It is designed to
 be fast, reliable, portable, and easy to use, and provides a rich SQL
 dialect with support for complex queries, window functions, and direct
 querying of Parquet, CSV, and JSON files.
 .
 This package ships the duckdb command line client, built following the
 official Linux release parameters: bundled extension set (parquet, json,
 icu, autocomplete) plus statically linked httpfs and sqlite/postgres/mysql
 scanner extensions (usable offline), jemalloc allocator, and the official
 x86-64-v3 optimization profile (requires an AVX2-capable CPU).
